<%# The turn-posting form. Shown only to the current_turn_user; every other viewer sees
    a note instead (waiting / spectator / concluded — see the three-way branch below).
    VIEWER-SCOPED: takes an explicit `viewer:` local, because `current_user` is
    undefined in a broadcast render context and using it here would blank the composer
    on every broadcast. Local: debate, viewer (defaults to current_user in the request
    context). Wrapped in the pinned dom_id so the Turbo-Stream replace lands here — the
    debate_composer controller refocuses the field on both first paint and that
    post-turn replace.

    PILL COMPOSER (Hoojah 2026, redesign Phase 3, Task 3.4) — mockup ~1141-1144: a pill
    textarea + a circular primary `send` button, replacing the boxed textarea + text
    submit. The textarea stays a `<textarea>`, not the mockup's literal `<input>`-style
    box — `field-sizing: content` (`.debate-composer-field`, `@layer components`) still
    needs a multi-line-capable element, and `rows` is still its min-height fallback
    where `field-sizing` is unsupported; only `rows` drops from 3 to 1 since a pill is a
    single visual line until content grows it. `debate-composer-target="field"` and
    `data-controller="debate-composer"` stay on the same elements as before (the
    Stimulus controller's `connect()` refocus does not change).

    The submit control is now an ICON-ONLY circular button (`f.button` + the `send`
    glyph, no visible label) rather than `f.submit "Post turn"` — `aria-label` carries
    the accessible name instead of a text node. `Capybara.enable_aria_label = true`
    (spec/support/capybara.rb) is what keeps every existing `click_button "Post turn"`
    in the system specs working unchanged against this button.

    Three non-form states, viewer-scoped by participancy (Task 3.5 adds the middle one):
      - the OTHER participant, mid-debate: "Waiting for @mover…" (unchanged copy).
      - a SPECTATOR (a present-but-non-participant viewer, or nil/logged-out) on an
        ACTIVE debate: "The verdict opens when the debate concludes." — the read-only
        affordance the spectator view (Task 3.5) needs in place of a turn form. A
        concluded debate's verdict is a SEPARATE, later task (3.6); this note only
        promises it opens, it does not render it.
      - CONCLUDED, any viewer: "This debate has concluded." (unchanged copy).
    All three stay plain 14px-muted centred sentences with no card behind them, exactly
    as before this task. %>
<% viewer = local_assigns.fetch(:viewer) { current_user } %>
<div id="<%= dom_id(debate, :composer) %>" class="my-4">
  <% if debate.active? && debate.current_turn_user == viewer %>
    <%= render layout: "ui/card", locals: {class: "p-3", data: {controller: "debate-composer"}} do %>
      <%= form_with url: debate_turns_path(debate.slug), method: :post, class: "flex items-end gap-2.5" do |f| %>
        <%= f.text_area :body, rows: 1, required: true, "aria-label": "Your turn",
              data: {"debate-composer-target": "field"},
              placeholder: "Make your argument…",
              class: "debate-composer-field flex-1 min-w-0 resize-none rounded-3xl border border-hairline bg-card-2 px-4 py-2.5 text-sm text-ink focus:outline-none focus:border-primary" %>
        <%= f.button type: "submit", "aria-label": "Post turn",
              class: "w-11 h-11 shrink-0 rounded-full bg-primary text-white shadow flex items-center justify-center active:scale-95 transition disabled:opacity-50" do %>
          <%= lucide_icon("send", class: "w-5 h-5") %>
        <% end %>
      <% end %>
    <% end %>
  <% elsif debate.active? && debate.participant?(viewer) %>
    <p class="text-grey text-center py-3">Waiting for @<%= debate.current_turn_user&.username %>…</p>
  <% elsif debate.active? %>
    <p class="text-grey text-center py-3">The verdict opens when the debate concludes.</p>
  <% elsif debate.concluded? %>
    <p class="text-grey text-center py-3">This debate has concluded.</p>
  <% end %>
</div>
